# MayBeString: `${value}`, with nothing known of the value. In line: is it a cell, is it a string, else the stub: 21 bytes a site at 80,752 sites of a large application. The stub asks the same two questions first.
# MEASURED (one binary, a byte at the door): by the stub everywhere that application's code is 1.59 MB smaller and its build 1.5 G cheaper, the TypeScript compiler checking a project runs 37.557 | 37.572 G, 335 rows x1.0001,
# and one row that converts in a hot loop loses 1.5%. So in a loop the two questions stay in line: openIn = Loop.
